    hook: "Abstract algebra studies operations and the structures they generate: groups, rings, fields, modules, and the morphisms that keep the operations honest. It is mathematics about what is preserved when the names change.",
    claim: "A group is the algebra of symmetry; a ring, of number-like addition and multiplication; a field, of a world where one may divide. Homomorphisms are the maps that matter. [[category-theory|Category theory]] later said this even more abstractly; [[noether|Noether]] had already made the subject modern.",
    scene: "Galois, the night before a duel, writing about groups of substitutions that decide whether a quintic is solvable. A student meeting the first isomorphism theorem and feeling the floor move.",
