    title: "Botany",
    hook: "Botany is the science of plants — the silent majority of visible life, and the engineers of air and soil. A biology that only notices animals has misunderstood the planet.",
    claim: "Photosynthetic sessile organisms with iterated modular bodies, meristems, and a chemistry that invented lignin, alkaloids, and the flower. [[photosynthesis|Photosynthesis]] is the energy thesis; [[ecology|ecology]] is the community thesis; [[linnaeus|Linnaeus]] is the naming thesis.",
    scene: "A herbarium sheet; a rainforest canopy; a field of wheat that is an evolutionary pact with Homo sapiens. The [[agricultural-revolution|agricultural revolution]] is botany as history.",
    origin: "Theophrastus, herbals, Linnaeus's sexual system, Brown's nucleus and Brownian motion, Darwin's orchids and climbing plants, Mendel's peas as genetics before genetics, the molecular plant labs of the late twentieth century.",
    work: "Floras, physiological ecology, Arabidopsis as a model, mycorrhizal networks, crop science. The public meets botany as gardening and as famine.",
    quarrel: "Plant intelligence: signaling, memory, behavior without a brain. The words inflame; the data (electrical, chemical, developmental) are real. Another quarrel: conservation versus yield.",
