    claim: "Scaling laws (Bettencourt, West) that make wages, crime, and patents rise superlinearly with size, and infrastructure sublinearly. Flows of food, water, power, data. [[scale-free-networks|Scale-free]] commuting and contact. [[stigmergy|Stigmergy]] of streets worn into being. The [[industrial-revolution|Industrial Revolution]] made the modern city; the city then made the rest.",
